Z||000000||Flywagon||06-02-2000||01:50 AM||||I pulled up to a lite in my '84 2m4 Coupe with 3 speed auto and the 41.1 gearing.  This green Stratus pulls up besides me and gives it a rev and looks at me like he is gonna kick my butt.  So I rev back, and wait.  The light on the other street changed to yellow, so I put her into neutral and reved up to like 3500rmp.  As soon as the light turned green, I dropped it back into drive and did a big burnout.  I took the stratus up to like 95mph and then backed off, because I was lke ten to twelve car lengths ahead!  It was a good day today.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||IamFast2m4||06-02-2000||01:54 AM||||How did you get that much gears?  I want more gears in my Fierro too.  did you install them yourself&gt;??  Nice kill dude!  Peopel dont' mess with me anymore since I put the Vtec sticker on my window.  They always ask me"is that a real vtek?"  I say "yes" and they won't reace anymore!  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||CUTTER||06-02-2000||03:53 AM||||what ever you do dont put it in neutral rev it and throw it in drive, it called "neutral droping" Its VERY bad for the transmition and i have proof. If you look at my trans its not the stock 87GT outa a fiero, its from a 84 pontiac 6000. I did that about 20 times and 1st gear started missing. Then a week later 2nd gear was missing. Then a month later I totally burned out 2nd gear. I was only running on 1st and 3rd gears. I was lucky the junk yard had a tranny for me and installed and everything for $450. Just warning you, dont neutral drop the tranny!||||reg||1
